On the way home, I go into the pharmacy.
I walk slowly because my head still hurts.
It is quiet and warm in the pharmacy.
A pharmacist is standing behind the counter.
"Good morning," I say and give her my green prescription.
She reads the prescription and nods.
"One moment please," she says and fetches the medicine.
She places a small box on the counter.
"You should take one tablet three times a day," she explains.
"Ideally after eating, with a glass of water."
I nod because I understand that well.
"How much does the medicine cost?" I ask.
"That will be seven euros, please," she answers.
I open my wallet and pay in cash.
The pharmacist gives me the medicine and the receipt.
"Get well soon!" she says warmly.
"Thank you very much," I answer.
I leave the pharmacy and walk the last streets home.
I am looking forward to my bed because I really do not feel well.
